# Sketchbook: the drawing vocabulary used the way an explanation uses it.
# Shapes that draw themselves, labels that find their own room, a part that
# changes into another, a group copied, a thing travelling along a curve.

look chalk
scene lever figure lines=2
line beam 14,50 86,50 thick=2
poly pivot 38,62 44,50 50,62 fill=accent
rect load 72,40 12x10 fill=dim
path push stroke=accent thick=1.5 | M20 26 V46 m-4 -5 l4 5 l4 -5
say label near=pivot:below | pivot
say label near=load:above | load
say | Push down far from the pivot and the short end lifts the load.
wait
poly pivot 62,62 68,50 74,62
say strong | Move the pivot closer: *less effort, less lift*.
wait 2

scene orbit caption lines=1
look blueprint
circle star 80,45 7 fill=accent stroke=none
ellipse track 80,45 46x24 stroke=dim thick=0.5
circle planet 126,45 3 fill=ink stroke=none
move planet along=track slow
say | A year is one trip round the track.
group moon at=34,45 loop=spin
circle in=moon 0,0 2 fill=alt stroke=none
line in=moon 0,0 6,0 stroke=dim thick=0.4
use moon2 moon at=118,30 scale=0.7
wait 3

scene shapes caption playful brisk
look riso
circle blob 80,42 16 fill=accent
say | One shape
circle blob 80,42 24 fill=alt
say | becomes another
poly blob 56,60 80,18 104,60 fill=ink
say | and another.
ambient confetti
wait 2

scene choices layout=caption
look paper
card c1 | Words stay in their card
say x48 in=c1 | Which shape has three sides?
say x50 choice in=c1 | Triangle
say x52 choice in=c1 | Square
say x54 aside | Choices in a card stand apart, each a target of its own.
wait 2
